\par}
{\tc\tcl3 \v Step-2 (Run on Windows, Can Effect on WSL)}
If {\f2 .gitignore}  is missing, run {\f2 2-create-git-ignore.bat}  to (re)create it.\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAACB}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAACB}
{{\pard\plain \s3\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\cgrid 
Step-3 (Only Windows)
\par}
{\tc\tcl3 \v Step-3 (Only Windows)}
Install package managers used by the next step: run {\f2 3-install-package-manager.bat}  (installs Chocolatey and Scoop).\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAACC}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAACC}
{{\pard\plain \s3\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\cgrid 
Step-4 (Only Windows)
\par}
{\tc\tcl3 \v Step-4 (Only Windows)}
Run {\f2 4-install-windows-enviroment.bat}  (as Administrator) to install CMake, Ninja, Doxygen, ReportGenerator, OpenCppCoverage, coverxygen, lcov ({\f2 genhtml} ), and the mkdocs toolchain.\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAACD}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAACD}
{{\pard\plain \s3\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\cgrid 
Step-5 (Only WSL)
\par}
{\tc\tcl3 \v Step-5 (Only WSL)}
Open the WSL Ubuntu terminal, go to the project folder, and run {\f2 4-install-wsl-environment.sh} . It also installs a per-user, current .NET SDK (needed by ReportGenerator - see docs/guide/troubleshooting.en.md if {\f2 dotnet} /{\f2 reportgenerator}  still resolve to an old version afterwards).\par}
\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAACE}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAACE}
{{\pard\plain \s2\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs28\kerning28\cgrid 
Generate Development Environment
\par}
{\tc\tcl2 \v Generate Development Environment}
Run {\f2 9-clean-configure-app-windows.bat}  to (re)configure the CMake project (Visual Studio if installed, otherwise Ninja).\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAACF}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAACF}
{{\pard\plain \s2\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs28\kerning28\cgrid 
Build, Test and Package Application on Windows
\par}
{\tc\tcl2 \v Build, Test and Package Application on Windows}
Run {\f2 7-build-app-windows.bat}  to build, test, generate every report (native + ReportGenerator), and package the application on Windows.\par
Also {\f2 7-build-doc-windows.bat}  to only (re)generate documentation/doc-coverage, and {\f2 8-build-test-windows.bat}  to only build and test.\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAACG}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAACG}
{{\pard\plain \s2\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs28\kerning28\cgrid 
Build, Test and Package Application on WSL
\par}
{\tc\tcl2 \v Build, Test and Package Application on WSL}
Run {\f2 7-build-app-linux.sh}  for the same pipeline on Linux/WSL. {\b Run it from a path under WSL's own filesystem}  (e.g. {\f2 ~/work/cpp-cmake-ctest-template} ), not a Windows Google-Drive-synced path - WSL cannot reach those; see docs/guide/install.en.md.\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAACH}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAACH}
{{\pard\plain \s2\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs28\kerning28\cgrid 
Open the site
\par}
{\tc\tcl2 \v Open the site}
{\f2 9-open-site.bat}  / {\f2 9-open-site.sh}  start a tiny local HTTP server over the built {\f2 site/}  folder and open it in your browser (falls back to the Doxygen API docs if the site has not been built yet). A real HTTP server, not {\f2 {\field {\*\fldinst { HYPERLINK "file://" }{}}{\fldrslt {\cs37\ul\cf2 file://}}}
} , is required because every report page embeds its report in an {\f2 <iframe>} , and most browsers block iframes from {\f2 {\field {\*\fldinst { HYPERLINK "file://" }{}}{\fldrslt {\cs37\ul\cf2 file://}}}
}  pages - see docs/guide/reports-in-site.en.md. Press {\f2 Ctrl+C}  in that terminal to stop the server when you are done.\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAACI}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAACI}
{{\pard\plain \s2\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs28\kerning28\cgrid 
Publish a release
\par}
{\tc\tcl2 \v Publish a release}
{\f2 10-release.bat} /{\f2 .sh}  build everything, package it (including the whole site as {\f2 site.zip} ), and publish it as a GitHub Release with the GitHub CLI ({\f2 gh} ) - works on a private repository with GitHub Free, uses no GitHub Actions minutes. Add {\f2 --dry-run}  to preview without publishing. See docs/guide/releases.en.md for {\f2 gh}  setup, the Student Developer Pack, and adding a collaborator so a private release is visible for grading.\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAACJ}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAACJ}
{{\pard\plain \s2\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs28\kerning28\cgrid 
Clean Project
\par}
{\tc\tcl2 \v Clean Project}
Run {\f2 9-clean-project.bat}  (Windows) or {\f2 9-clean-project.sh}  (Linux/WSL) to remove every generated output folder.\par}
